--- Section 3: Structural Analysis of Scaling ---

STRUCTURAL RESULT: kappa_H/T_eff is NOT a pure power law of Ma.
  kappa_H ~ Ma^1 (velocity gradient scales linearly with v)
  r_k ~ Ma (squeeze linear in sudden limit)
  nbar = sinh^2(r) ~ exp(2r)/4 for r >> 1 (exponential in Ma)
  T_eff ~ omega * nbar ~ omega * exp(2*r_0*Ma/Ma_phys) (exponential)
  => kappa/T_eff ~ Ma * exp(-2*r_0*Ma/Ma_phys) (DECREASING)

Individual scaling fits (Ma in [1, 20]):
  kappa_H(Ma) = 65.08 * Ma^0.8027 +/- 0.0116
  T_eff(Ma)   = 0.0000 * Ma^9.1091 +/- 0.1018
  kappa/T_eff = 584.4853 * Ma^-0.8440 +/- 0.0681

